rs/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/d8335f2a6ee4194baf6ba786422986bc74d568f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:02:23Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:02:23Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"fix(chores): replace fabricated category chart with a real status breakdown\n\nThe Insights \"Category Distribution\" donut chart derived a fake\ncategory (Kitchen/Plants & Garden/Pets/Living Room) by pattern-matching\nthe first two hex characters of each chore instance''s randomly\ngenerated template_id UUID. ChoreTemplate has no category concept at\nall, so the chart was presenting statistically meaningless noise as a\nreal household insight.\n\nRather than inventing a category field with no product design behind\nit, the chart now shows today''s chores broken down by their actual,\nalready-tracked status (completed/pending/missed) -- a real property\nof the data instead of a fabricated one.\n\nFixes #502","tree":{"sha":"307b9541d6c0b5f99e7ad15bfbc1eef076b4db11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/307b9541d6c0b5f99e7ad15bfbc1eef076b4db11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/d8335f2a6ee4194baf6ba786422986bc74d568f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/d8335f2a6ee4194baf6ba786422986bc74d568f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSdRjLtoAKGQ4MzM1ZjJhNmVlNDE5NGJhZjZiYTc4NjQyMjk4NmJjNzRkNTY4ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/f89ddd6f4710cac317def2e82fc4721baaf48224","sha":"f89ddd6f4710cac317def2e82fc4721baaf48224","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/f89ddd6f4710cac317def2e82fc4721baaf48224"}],"sha":"d8335f2a6ee4194baf6ba786422986bc74d568f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/d8335f2a6ee4194baf6ba786422986bc74d568f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/f89ddd6f4710cac317def2e82fc4721baaf48224/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:02:00Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:02:00Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"fix(chores): verify assignees are household members before assigning\n\nPOST /api/v1/chores/instances/{id}/assign and the assign_chore MCP\ntool stored assigned_to on the instance with no check that the id\nbelonged to an actual member of the caller''s household -- only the\ncaller''s own membership (via require_household) and the OWNER/ADMIN\nelevation for assigning someone else were checked.\n\nBoth paths now confirm the target is a household member before\npersisting:\n\n- The REST endpoint uses the same get_membership_lookup dependency\n  require_household is built on, checking the target UUID as a\n  candidate subject. This is exact whenever the assignee''s OIDC\n  subject is itself a UUID (the common case here); a non-member id\n  (including a random UUID) is rejected with 404.\n- The MCP tool has the caller-supplied assignee_user_id before it is\n  derived into a UUID, so it checks membership against that raw\n  sub/id directly via the same shared membership client the MCP\n  authentication middleware uses.\n\nSelf-assignment (claim/release, where the target is always the\ncaller''s own id) never triggers the check, so it can''t regress the\nclaim flow.\n\nFixes #513","tree":{"sha":"21158fe49ce509f8dc1a0ed0abe5e8513640cacd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/21158fe49ce509f8dc1a0ed0abe5e8513640cacd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/f89ddd6f4710cac317def2e82fc4721baaf48224","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuse