if","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/c2823f28ba376ef30187bd835af2c86eff5d5926/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:01:51Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T22:01:51Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"fix(chores): self-heal streak across real multi-day gaps\n\nensure_household_reset only ever looked at target_date - 1 day. If a\nhousehold (or the nightly scheduler itself) misses more than one full\nday, the skipped days never get instance rows, yesterday''s query comes\nback empty, and the whole missed-evaluation branch was skipped\nentirely -- the streak silently survived the absence.\n\nWalk back to whichever day actually has instances instead of assuming\nit''s always yesterday, and treat any day strictly in between as fully\nmissed for streak purposes (without backfilling instance rows for\nthose days, to avoid rewriting history or double counting). This fixes\nboth the app-level case (nobody opens the app for days) and the\nscheduler-level case (the nightly job itself was down for days) with\nthe same fix, since both surface as \"the last known day is more than\none day before target_date\".\n\nFixes #507","tree":{"sha":"73e9569511ad179b688990ddfa9e0449c3b86025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/73e9569511ad179b688990ddfa9e0449c3b86025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commi