m","name":"Leif"},"message":"docs(explanation): document core/household and correct the shopping-502 theory\n\n- architecture-overview.md: core/ held two Tier-1 apps (dashboard and\n  household) with no mention of household anywhere on the page; add it to\n  the monorepo layout, the control-plane section (with what the dashboard\n  no longer owns) and core-net\n- known-issues.md: shopping''s suspected 502 root cause said \"no mem_limit\n  is set for shopping-frontend\" — every frontend, not just shopping, is\n  capped at memory: 128m in compose.prod.yaml, so the suspected cause is\n  an OOM kill under that fleet-wide limit, not a shopping-specific gap;\n  also add the shopping default-list side effect and the workout offline\n  sync household-at-flush-time entries\n- create-new-fdd-service.md: the tutorial never mentioned household\n  authorization at all, told readers to add a dedicated database\n  container even though every new app since budget/library shares\n  postgres-core, and its one Caddy example reverse-proxied a backend onto\n  a frontend path. Rewrite to require_household/require_role,\n  HOUSEHOLD_INTERNAL_URL/ALFHEIM_INTERNAL_TOKEN wiring,\n  HouseholdProvider/HouseholdGate on the frontend, the shared-Postgres\n  registration in init-multiple-dbs.sh, and a correct paired\n  frontend+backend Caddy example matching the existing per-app pattern","tree":{"sha":"5d8e344db6b4039d817f2992b162d6827b802bba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/5d8e344db6b4039d817f2992b162d6827b802bba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/fb806b0082ff6e1d013d18bc23250c686c7eac20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/fb806b0082ff6e1d013d18bc23250c686c7eac20","node_id":"C_kwDOSdRjLtoAKGZiODA2YjAwODJmZjZlMWQwMTNkMThiYzIzMjUwYzY4NmM3ZWFjMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa","sha":"96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa"}],"sha":"fb806b0082ff6e1d013d18bc23250c686c7eac20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/fb806b0082ff6e1d013d18bc23250c686c7eac20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:48Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:48Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"docs(how-to): make the dev test-token guide actually mint a working token\n\nThe published guide never signed the JWT it told readers to exchange:\nStep 3''s Node snippet logged \"JWT created\" without calling a signing\nfunction, and \\${JWT} was never assigned anywhere before Step 4 used it.\nFollowing the guide verbatim produces an empty assertion and a token\nexchange that fails.\n\nReplace it with a dependency-free procedure verified end to end (a local\nRSA key, openssl-signed RS256 assertion, and the actual base64url\nencode/decode and openssl dgst -sign/-verify round trip were all run and\nchecked before writing this):\n\n- create the machine user and a JSON key via Zitadel''s Management API v1\n  using the bootstrap PAT, matching how alfheim-setup provision\n  authenticates\n- build and sign the JWT profile assertion with openssl and jq only (no\n  Node, no JWT library): iss = sub = the machine user id, aud = the\n  issuer, kid = the key''s keyId\n- resolve the token endpoint from OIDC discovery instead of guessing\n  /oauth/token vs /oauth/v2/token, exchange it for an access token with\n  the jwt-bearer grant and the project-audience scope, and use\n  --data-urlencode instead of a hand-rolled %20\n- expanded Troubleshooting section covering signature/kid mismatches and\n  what to do if Zitadel''s Management API response shape has changed","tree":{"sha":"788f61954e89dbf605d45db5be02befb87927695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/788f61954e89dbf605d45db5be02befb87927695"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa","node_id":"C_kwDOSdRjLtoAKDk2MDA3MjIxMjY4MjU2ZTRkYTMwNWEyZDIwNjY1YmQxZDk5NDRiZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e","sha":"36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e"}],"sha":"96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/96007221268256e4da305a2d20665bd1d9944bfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:35Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:35Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"docs(how-to): fix commands that referenced containers and vars that don''t exist\n\n- backup-restore.md: there is no per-app database container\n  (alfheim_<app>_db) — every service database lives in the single\n  alfheim_postgres_core container. Fix every dump/restore command to\n  target alfheim_postgres_core with the real alfheim_<app> database name,\n  add alfheim_household to the dump-everything loop, and correct the\n  volume names to their Compose-project-prefixed form\n  (alfheim-prod_postgres_core_data, alfheim-prod_rustfs_data)\n- update-installation.md: remove the fabricated \"or set -e in a script\"\n  aside (bash''s own set -e does nothing for the installer''s confirmation\n  prompt); document the real triggers for update mode instead\n  (ALFHEIM_UPDATE=1, a leading \"update\" argument, or an existing\n  .alfheim.installed with no arguments at all)\n- troubleshooting.md: fix two container names (pantry-frontend has no\n  alfheim_ prefix; the Postgres commands need alfheim_postgres_core and\n  the alfheim_pantry database, not a nonexistent alfheim_pantry_db)\n- secrets-hardening.md: the per-service Postgres password variable is\n  <APP>_POSTGRES_PASSWORD (e.g. PANTRY_POSTGRES_PASSWORD), not\n  <app>_DB_PASSWORD, which does not exist anywhere in the codebase","tree":{"sha":"9fc6679f9387f14de7f4d66f71097899c4fb7292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/9fc6679f9387f14de7f4d66f71097899c4fb7292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e","node_id":"C_kwDOSdRjLtoAKDM2YmFmMGFlNDhjN2VhZTY0MGYyMmJkNjhkNjBkM2VjODRlZTFkOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/ab54a2759b52382535e282498434076bd2178378","sha":"ab54a2759b52382535e282498434076bd2178378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/ab54a2759b52382535e282498434076bd2178378"}],"sha":"36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/36baf0ae48c7eae640f22bd68d60d3ec84ee1d9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/ab54a2759b52382535e282498434076bd2178378/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:18Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:32:18Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"docs(apps): make every app reference page a real app-sprint starting point\n\nEvery docs/*/reference/apps/*.md now covers MCP tools, household scoping\nand a Known Issues & Open Follow-Ups section, so each app sprint starts\nfrom an accurate baseline instead of re-deriving this from source first.\n\n- Add MCP tool tables (with function names from the actual mcp_tools.py /\n  server.py files) to pantry, chores, maintenance, budget, library, chat\n  and workout; note explicitly where an app has no MCP server (shopping,\n  budget, library) or only a placeholder tool (library''s\n  get_library_status)\n- shopping: document the GET /shopping-lists side effect (creates the\n  household''s default list and the caller''s personal list on first call)\n  and the Proxmox 502 (fleet-wide 128m frontend memory limit, unconfirmed\n  root cause, not shopping-specific)\n- workout: document that the offline sync queue replays against whichever\n  household is active when it flushes, not the household active when the\n  set was logged\n- library: correct the purpose table and domain feature list to match the\n  actual API modules (items, lending, locations, lookup, manuals,\n  providers, search) — the previously documented reading-progress log and\n  household wishlist do not exist anywhere in the backend or frontend\n  source\n- household, dashboard: add a Known Issues section (membership cache\n  staleness, 503 on an unavailable household service; dashboard is a\n  launcher now, with its own future app sprint)","tree":{"sha":"12f1b64ee2fe1d75c00222fc3eae5ca221027903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/12f1b64ee2fe1d75c00222fc3eae5ca221027903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/commits/ab54a2759b52382535e282498434076bd2178378","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","followi