NjNDIxMzJiYWRlNTMwMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/4d0edbcc29369279204c64d6fa9fa2e5de98a577","sha":"4d0edbcc29369279204c64d6fa9fa2e5de98a577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/4d0edbcc29369279204c64d6fa9fa2e5de98a577"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commit/843633fb0e8b396c28002a2e49a8261361753b47","sha":"843633fb0e8b396c28002a2e49a8261361753b47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/843633fb0e8b396c28002a2e49a8261361753b47"}],"sha":"af475af416d74f1f60cb9b283c42132bade53001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/af475af416d74f1f60cb9b283c42132bade53001"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174730541?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KroegerLeif","id":174730541,"login":"KroegerLeif","node_id":"U_kgDOCmotLQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/843633fb0e8b396c28002a2e49a8261361753b47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T15:49:31Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T15:49:31Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"feat(installer): add alfheim-setup update for one-command releases\n\nAdds an explicit `alfheim-setup update [--version vX.Y.Z] [--install-dir DIR]\n[--yes]` entry point so an owner can go from a fresh install to every later\nrelease with one command, without re-running the wizard, regenerating\nsecrets, or touching the root CA, the Zitadel machinekey/PAT or a Docker\nvolume.\n\nIt requires an existing installation, resolves the target version from\n--version or this binary''s own build version (never \"latest\"), downloads and\nchecksum-verifies that release''s standalone stack files (internal/shared/\nassets.StackAssets), backs up the previous copies to a timestamped\ndirectory, sets IMAGE_TAG in .env, then reuses the existing Day-2 logic\n(backfill missing secrets, re-provision Zitadel, ensure every service\ndatabase) before pulling images and restarting with --remove-orphans. On\nfailure it prints the concrete rollback steps.\n\ninstall.sh gains matching support: ALFHEIM_UPDATE=1, a leading \"update\"\nargument, or an existing installation with no arguments hand off to\n`alfheim-setup update --version <resolved tag>` after downloading that\nrelease''s binary.\n\nA release build''s fresh-install default image tag is now its own version\nrather than \"latest\" (dev builds keep \"latest\").\n\nAdds scripts/verify-stack.sh (compose service health, Caddy /livez, OIDC\ndiscovery issuer, every app route, /internal/* blocked at the edge, the\nhousehold API''s 401 without a token), works against either compose.prod.yaml\nor the dev compose.yaml, and ships as a release asset like the other\nstandalone stack files.\n\nDocs: docs/{en,de}/how-to/update-installation.md, linked from the installer\nCLI reference and the first-run tutorial''s \"Updating later\" section.","tree":{"sha":"363050ebbc1712ec4f60670604b462fa25ba636f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/363050ebbc1712ec4f60670604b462fa25ba636f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/