","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KroegerLeif","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/commits/746b1e0bcdfa6af286fd46a7595985f4f6b5b2b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T08:39:57Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T08:39:57Z","email":"Leif.kr@outlook.com","name":"Leif"},"message":"refactor(maintenance): UUID households from core/household\n\nHouseholds are owned by core/household. Drop the local household table and\nits FK; device.household_id is now an indexed UUID column. All routes use\nbackend_shared.household.require_household (the maintenance wizard and\nsummary endpoints previously had no auth at all and the summary leaked every\nhousehold). GET /households is kept (deprecated) and returns only the\nX-Household-ID household. DeviceCreate no longer carries household_id.\n\nMCP tools read the household from get_mcp_household_context(). BudgetClient\nand the shopping supply bridge forward the caller''s bearer token and the UUID\nX-Household-ID. init_db refuses to start on the legacy integer schema with\nreset instructions instead of auto-migrating (schema comes from create_all).\n\nTests use UUID households and the shared testing helpers and cover 400/401/\n403/503, cross-tenant isolation and the legacy-schema guard.","tree":{"sha":"538245665b7d1d04a0d14f17f0a40a38787f8030","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/trees/538245665b7d1d04a0d14f17f0a40a38787f8030"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KroegerLeif/Alfheim/git/