hor":{"date":"2026-05-16T17:10:48Z","email":"gowthambalashanmugam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"gauti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T17:10:48Z","email":"gowthambalashanmugam@users.noreply.github.com","name":"gauti"},"message":"feat: Add requirements and tasks for stabilizing subscription leak detector\n\n- Introduced requirements document outlining key features for the subscription leak detector, including build compilation, deterministic issue IDs, false positive reduction, runtime safety, and test coverage.\n- Created tasks document detailing actionable items to implement the requirements, including fixing build errors, ensuring null safety, stabilizing the subscription leak detector, setting up Vitest for testing, and final verification steps.\n\nchore: Update repository links in documentation\n\n- Updated all instances of repository links in various markdown files to point to the new nglens organization.\n- Ensured consistency across CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md, and other relevant documents.\n\nfix: Improve security measures in overlay renderer and popup\n\n- Added HTML escaping functions to prevent XSS vulnerabilities when rendering component names and issue descriptions in overlays and popup UI.\n- Enhanced the rendering logic to utilize the new escape functions for safer output.\n\nrefactor: Stabilize issue ID generation in subscription leak detector\n\n- Implemented a stable hash function for generating deterministic issue IDs based on component names and leak types.\n- Introduced checks for known cleanup patterns to reduce false positives in leak detection.\n\nstyle: Adjust SVG text positioning in popup\n\n- Modified the positioning of SVG text elements in the popup to improve visual alignment and readability.\n\nfeat: Add icons for extension\n\n- Added new icon files (icon16.png, icon48.png, icon128.png) for the extension to enhance its appearance in the Chrome Web Store.","tree":{"sha":"c57763588e0e770e13b1ab842fbc9f81ad5e310d","